it's been just over a week since I  switched to the iPhone 11 Pro max after  using the tennis max for practically a  year and today I'm gonna tell you every  real-world difference that I noticed  some that Apple advertised and I was  expecting and others that I wasn't but  really surprised me and even a few  disappointments let's jump right in and  I'll put it right out there the biggest  difference that actually affects my  daily life and solely makes the iPhone  11 Pro worth the upgrade from the 10s  and that is the battery life yes Apple  finally put a fast charger in the box  but at this point that doesn't even  matter at all there is no need for it  I've never had to top off my 11 Pro max  and after a week that is literally  providing a sense of relief or maybe  even freedom not having to worry about  what my battery life is that we're  having to check it throughout the day I  use my phone a lot from tons of emails  notifications YouTube videos music  podcasts and multiple apps that track my  location in the background for security  and home automation  so my iPhones battery really gets  hammered I start using my phone at about  7 a.m. and I would always have to top  off my tennis Max's battery by about 6  or 7 or else the battery would die let's  just say that I was shocked the first  night when I set it to charge at 10:00  p.m. and the battery was that 26% the  next night it was at 30% just after  10:00 p.m. and the following night I  plugged it in around midnight and it was  at 20% I have never had any flagship  smartphone performed this good while  being pushed so hard next is the matte  glass back it looks fantastic it  actually looks like gold this time and I  love that it's basically fingerprint  proof but my issue with it is that it's  much more slippery than the glossy glass  back of the iPhone 10's max  I don't use cases on my phones so that  was definitely something that was  noticeable I have to be a lot more  careful with it on hold when holding in  my hand and grip it tighter because it's  way more slippery on the front  I love the display brightness the  readability is so much better in bright  Sun it's more pleasant to use and makes  a massive difference if you use your  phone as a display for a drone  controller next let's talk about the  speakers the 10s sounded really good but  I did wish that we had more volume  particularly in loud environments and  Apple definitely stepped it up even a  week later I'm still being surprised by  them when  opening up a high quality sounding video  or podcast what surprised me even more  is when I watched the portion of the  movie 300 on iTunes I was shocked by how  good the fake surround sound is both a  separation of channels as well as  individual sound effects sound  impossibly good for a tiny thin  smartphone not that this is important in  daily use but it definitely jumped out  at me and it's something that I can  appreciate another thing that stood out  to me is the sound quality of the  earpiece speaker most of us don't talk  about call quality which we definitely  need to change but the higher quality  and louder earpiece speaker makes a  noticeable difference but it doesn't  stop there  the first time I called my wife on the  pro with her using the new 11 she  immediately mentioned how good the call  quality was and I definitely noticed it  it was an even bigger difference than  talking to other people since it seems  that either the microphone or the voice  processing has been noticeably improved  it was an even bigger difference than  when talking to other people since it  seems that either the microphone and/or  the voice processing has been improved  but either way calls are louder and  clearer now before I tell you about how  the camera updates stand out in the real  world and about a few disappointments  that presented themselves let me tell  you about our standout sponsor brilliant  really helps you excel in math and  science by actually solving problems and  learning concepts by applying them  instead of just listening to lectures  which in the real world works much  better  it's enjoyed by students professionals  in science enthusiasts all over the  world they have a wide range of content  like daily problems in math science and  computer science as well as interactive  courses from basic algebra all the way  to quantum computing now I personally  dislike learning math because many of my  classes were boring but when I could  work on real-world tasks that required  math or science I excelled and I had a  blast if that's you as well definitely  check out brilliant we're solving  problems can actually be so fun it's  addictive to support the channel and  learn more about brilliance go to  brilliant org slash Mac stack where you  can sign up for free and learn all kinds  of things and as a bonus for Mac's tech  viewers the first 200 people will also  get 20% off of their annual membership  now for the cameras everybody knows that  there is a big improvement but does it  change how you use the cameras and what  you  caPSURE in real life which might  actually be more important than an  increase in sharpness the answer is yes  first off the ultra wide lens allowed me  to capture certain shots I simply  wouldn't have been able to and also made  for some interesting perspectives second  is the much improved telephoto camera  previously I would straight-up avoid  using it and lower light situations  because the quality would be much worse  than the standard camera now not only  does a telephoto look dramatically  better in low light in the colors match  but we also have the option to take  portraits with the standard lens  this makes the iPhone 11 much more like  a real dedicated camera where you can  choose the lens's focal length based on  what fits the scene best and not what  you're forced to use with that comes the  selfie camera the quality is improved in  Apple's color processing is more  pleasing than before with more contrast  added which is great now I personally  haven't used a 4k 60 option but I did  find a useful time to do a slow fee  which isn't as bad as it sounds the  wider angle is definitely handy to fit  more people in the shots or just not to  have to hold it so far out away from you  now the camera app has also been  frustrating me it takes longer to open  sometimes just a little bit longer but  other times two to three times longer  and that's what the latest version of  iOS I never thought of myself as a huge  fan of 3d touch but now having it gone I  really miss it I would often use it to  quickly open the camera app the  flashlight deal with notifications and  more  unfortunately I highly doubt the Apple  will bring it back but this is kind of  the case of not knowing you love  something until it's gone I've heard  many people say that they didn't notice  a difference in performance since the  a12 Bionic processor is already so  powerful and while that is true I  personally did notice some differences a  part of this could definitely be faster  animations but it definitely launches  some apps faster and I saw the biggest  difference when I would quickly be  changing through multiple apps when  multitasking it is just so fluid and  quick the iPhone 11s have new Wi-Fi 6  built in but I haven't noticed any speed  differences probably because I don't  have a Wi-Fi 6 router and even if I did  my internet speed is probably limitation  but what I did notice is a smoother  transition between LTE and Wi-Fi and  vice-versa  with my iPhone 10 s if I would be  watching a video and switching data  connections I would often get  between a few seconds of buffering all  the way up to maybe 15 seconds at times  and sometimes I would even completely  have the video hang and I would have to  rewind a bit to get it going again now  this transition is noticeably smoother  and buffering is faster  unfortunately reception didn't get  better in the few parts of town I always  have issues with but it did notice  faster buffering and loading and YouTube  what issue I faced with my opponent  Ennis max is blue to delays both with my  car and with my smart lock I would walk  up to my house and some of the times I  would have to just stand there and wait  for it to connect and unlock we're now  with the iPhone 11 Pro it seems to  connect from further away these are the  kind of things that you won't see on a  spec sheet but are definitely noticeable  in real-life usage I'm very happy with  the upgrade from my iPhone 10s to the  iPhone 11 Pro sure it's not a massive  redesign but more of an iterative  upgrade with different things that make  the overall experience much better from  the different cameras with wider angles  and better quality to the massive jump  and battery life that would really help  heavy phone users like myself  this year's upgrade is better than what  people thought after the launch event if  you upgraded from an iPhone 10s to an 11  pro or even from a 10 let me know if you  noticed anything else down in the  comment section below and what your  favorite upgrade is click the little  circle above to subscribe and the bell  down below so you don't miss out on  future videos and if you want to see  Vadim's excellent iPhone 11 Pro review  click right over there this one max with  max tech and I will see you in the next  video  [Music]

